  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The following table shows the inflow rate of water, $q(t),$ in $\\text{L/min},$ into a storage tank over a period of $90$ minutes.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{minutes})$ | $0$ | $20$ | $60$ | $90$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $q(t)\\,(\\text{L/min})$ | $15$ | $25$ | $20$ | $10$ |\n\nUse the trapezoidal rule with the partition\n\n$$\n[0,20]\\cup [20,60]\\cup [60,90],\n$$\n\nto approximate the total volume of water that flowed into the tank in $90$ minutes.\n\nThe total volume is {{field-1}} liters.",
  "worked_solution": "In this context, we have $3$ trapezoids, and the area $A$ under the curve $y=q(t)$ represents the total volume of water that flowed into the tank in $90$ minutes.\n\nUsing the trapezoidal rule, we estimate the area as follows:\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{q(0)+q(20)}{2}\\cdot \u0394{t}_{1}+\\frac{q(20)+q(60)}{2}\\cdot \u0394{t}_{2}+\\frac{q(60)+q(90)}{2}\\cdot \u0394{t}_{3}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{15+25}{2}\\cdot (20-0)+\\frac{25+20}{2}\\cdot (60-20)+\\frac{20+10}{2}\\cdot (90-60) \\\\  & =20\\cdot 20+22.5\\cdot 40+15\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =400+900+450 \\\\  & =1750.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total volume of water that flowed into the tank is $1750$ liters.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
